    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 220\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n\nSenate Bill Number 6445, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  in  relation  to  legalizing,  validating,  ratifying  and\n      confirming a transportation contract of  the  Cold  Spring  Harbor\n      central school district\"\n\nSenate Bill Number 7344-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  validate  certain  acts of the Islip Union Free school\n      district with regard to certain capital improvement projects\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  Each of these bills would authorize, outside the State Budget process,\npayment of State education aid above the amounts calculated  and  previ-\nously agreed to under current law.\n\n  These  bills  would  validate  a  transportation  contract and capital\nimprovement state building aid for the Cold Spring Harbor Central School\nDistrict and Islip Union Free School District, respectively, even though\nboth districts failed to meet long-standing  statutory  requirements  of\naid eligibility.\n\n  Further,  each of these bills would result in increased and unbudgeted\nstate costs. Finally, Cold Spring Harbor's transportation contract falls\noutside the scope of forgiveness provisions negotiated by  the  Legisla-\nture  and  the  Executive  and  included  in the 2012-13 Enacted budget,\nthereby voiding that agreed upon  solution.  For  these  reasons,  these\nbills  should  necessarily  be  addressed in the context of enacting the\noverall state budget. I am therefore constrained to veto these bills.\n\n  The bills are disapproved.                  (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
